<!--
  BlockML Definition — block member meta-model base type

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.definition.MemberDefinition
  See docs/12_bom_object_model.md — MemberDefinitionBase · 02_mbml.md — Members.
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:bml="http://blockml.org/schema/bml">

  <idea>Abstract base for a declared member on a Block definition.</idea>

  <documentation>Abstract base type for Block member declarations — properties, aggregations,
    associations, and capabilities. Rendered as a child element inside the corresponding member
    container on BlockDefinition; the XML element name is the member name (bml:xml="${ #this.name }").
    An optional XML prefix on the element name supplies the member namespace — resolved via xmlns to
    BOM namespace; unprefixed elements use the default namespace (empty string). Member identity is
    (resolvedNamespace, localName). Inherits abstract and final modifiers from
    org.blockml.bml.definition.StructuralDefinition.

    Member value placement (scalar members on PropertyDefinition, CapabilityDefinition, and shared
    MemberDefinition fields):
    • On member declarations (Block definition documents): each member field may render as a child
      element or as an attribute on the member element — both are valid; element form is preferred
      when serializing definitions (e.g. &lt;type&gt;Integer&lt;/type&gt; over type="Integer").
    • On Block instances (composition): the same fields may also render as element or attribute —
      both are valid; attribute form is preferred when serializing instances (e.g. width="50" over
      &lt;width&gt;50&lt;/width&gt;).
    Structured children (constraints, suggestions, composition, implementation) remain elements.

    Member declaration modes are orthogonal:
    • new — introduces a new member; must not set override="true"
    • override="true" — refines an inherited member of the same identity (namespace + localName).
      override is local-only (not inherited) and does not change abstract/final semantics.

    Member completeness is expressed exclusively via the inherited abstract modifier:
    - abstract is inherited effectively; an inherited abstract="true" is lifted only by explicitly
      setting abstract="false" on a local redeclaration.
    - A transition abstract: true → false is the explicit implementation event of this member.
      In that local redeclaration, the required member-specific fields must be present locally
      (Property: type; Aggregation: type; Association: type; Capability: type + implementation).

    Maps to BOM MemberDefinitionBase fields shared by all member kinds — including visibility and
    readOnly attributes on member elements.</documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="12_bom_object_model.md">
      MemberDefinitionBase and member kind unions in the BOM.
    </see>
    <see file="02_mbml.md">
      Member containers, abstract/override/final rules.
    </see>
    <see block="def:BlockDefinition">
      Parent block shape — properties, aggregations, associations, capabilities containers.
    </see>
    <see block="def:ConstrainableDefinition">
      Shared constraints container for Block and member definitions.
    </see>
  </references>

  <name>MemberDefinition</name>
  <type>def:MemberDefinition</type>
  <baseType>def:ConstrainableDefinition</baseType>
  <abstract />
  <bml:xml>${ #this.name }</bml:xml>

  <properties>
    <abstract bml:xml="element|attribute">
      <value>false</value>
      <documentation>Overrides org.blockml.bml.definition.StructuralDefinition.abstract for member
        declarations (bml:xml="element|attribute"). On definitions, element form is preferred; on
        Block instances, attribute form is preferred. Semantics inherited from StructuralDefinition —
        member abstract marks an incomplete declaration that must be implemented by a descendant.</documentation>
    </abstract>
    <final bml:xml="element|attribute">
      <value>false</value>
      <documentation>Overrides org.blockml.bml.definition.StructuralDefinition.final for member
        declarations (bml:xml="element|attribute"). On definitions, element form is preferred; on
        Block instances, attribute form is preferred. Semantics inherited from StructuralDefinition —
        final members cannot be redeclared in child Blocks.</documentation>
    </final>
    <override bml:xml="element|attribute">
      <value>false</value>
      <documentation>When true, this member declaration overrides an inherited member of the same
        identity (namespace + localName). bml:xml="element|attribute" — on definitions, element
        form is preferred; on Block instances, attribute form is preferred. override is a local
        declaration statement and is not inherited. The validator requires a matching parent member
        in the baseType chain. A new member must not set override="true".

        override does not modify abstract or final. It may be used to change documentation or other
        optional metadata without implementing an abstract member.</documentation>
    </override>
    <visibility bml:xml="element|attribute">
      <documentation>Optional BlockML access visibility — private, protected, or public. Omitted =
        derived from the member element name: __ prefix → private, _ prefix → protected, otherwise
        public (BML_VISIBILITY_MISMATCH when explicit visibility does not match the naming
        convention). bml:xml="element|attribute" — on definitions, element form is preferred; on
        Block instances, attribute form is preferred. Controls BlockML authoring access — not
        renderer BOM access. On aggregations, visibility additionally controls composition instance
        ID reachability: public — bml:id values referencable via {EnclosingBlockFQN}::{id} from other
        documents; protected — ids reachable within the declaring Block and its child Blocks only;
        private — ids reachable within the declaring Block only. Maps to BOM
        MemberDefinitionBase.visibility.</documentation>
    </visibility>
    <readOnly bml:xml="element|attribute">
      <value>false</value>
      <documentation>When true, Block instances must not set this member (BML_READONLY_MEMBER_WRITE).
        Default false. bml:xml="element|attribute" — on definitions, element form is preferred; on
        Block instances, attribute form is preferred. Definition and child override may still supply
        values on the member declaration; readOnly forbids instance authoring only. Maps to BOM
        MemberDefinitionBase.readOnly.</documentation>
    </readOnly>
  </properties>

</block>
